+# Changes
+
+## Phase 1 · tokenizer
+
+Added `src/tokenize.mjs` implementing `tokenize(text)`:
+
+- Scans `text` left to right, producing `{ type, value, at }` tokens where
+  `type` is one of `number`, `op`, `lparen`, `rparen` and `at` is the index
+  of the token's first character.
+- Recognizes integers and decimals (`1`, `2.5`); a `.` lacking a digit on
+  either side throws a `SyntaxError` whose message names the index of the
+  `.`.
+- Recognizes operators `+ - * / ^` and parentheses `(` `)`; skips spaces,
+  tabs and newlines; any other character throws a `SyntaxError` naming its
+  index.
+- Throws a `TypeError` if `text` is not a string.
+
+`tests/tokenize.test.mjs` (pre-existing, not modified) passes: 4/4 tests,
+`npm test` exits 0 with nothing skipped or todo.
+
+## Phase 2 · evaluator
+
+Added `src/evaluate.mjs` implementing `evaluate(text)` as a recursive-descent
+parser built on `tokenize`:
+
+- Precedence, tightest to loosest: parentheses; `^` (right-associative);
+  unary minus; `*`/`/` (left-associative); `+`/`-` (left-associative). `^`
+  binds tighter than unary minus, so `-2 ^ 2` is `-4` and, being
+  right-associative, `2 ^ 3 ^ 2` is `512`.
+- Division by zero throws `RangeError`; any malformed expression (trailing
+  operator, doubled operand, unmatched parenthesis, stray operator where an
+  operand is expected, empty/whitespace-only input) throws `SyntaxError`
+  because the parser requires the whole token stream to reduce to a single
+  expression with nothing left over.
+- Unary minus recurses (`--2` is `2`, `-(1 + 2)` is `-3`), so chained or
+  parenthesized unary minus is well-defined rather than an error.
+- Non-string input and anything the tokenizer itself rejects (unknown
+  characters, bad numbers) surface as whatever error `tokenize` raises
+  (`TypeError` or `SyntaxError` naming the index); `evaluate` does not
+  reinterpret those.
+
+Added `tests/evaluate.test.mjs` covering the seven cases from the phase 2
+entry (`1 + 2 * 3` → `7`, `(1 + 2) * 3` → `9`, `2 ^ 3 ^ 2` → `512`,
+`-2 ^ 2` → `-4`, `10 / 4` → `2.5`, `1 / 0` → `RangeError`, `1 +` →
+`SyntaxError`) plus edge cases thought through from the entry: empty and
+whitespace-only input, two numbers with no operator between them, a stray
+`+` where an operand is expected (no unary plus), unmatched parentheses,
+chained unary minus, unary minus before a parenthesis, unary minus mixed
+with `*`/`/`, an unknown character, and non-string input.
+
+`npm test` passes: 20/20 tests, exit 0, nothing skipped or todo.
